Package: @alchemy.run/domain
Applies-to: vendor/alchemy/alchemy.run-domain-e1c3e6d.tgz
Upstream: not yet reported
Why: The prover reads `State.make({...})` of a struct as the fields written and nothing more, where the library's
  `make` adds each field left out that has a constructor default (`Schema.withConstructorDefault`, and the tag of
  `Schema.tag`). A state built that way is "read wrongly" for every rule, so an `evolve` has to write every field,
  the status and each count that starts at zero included, and the schema's defaults cannot be used. With this a
  field left out takes its default when that is a number, a text, a truth or `null` already there
  (`Effect.succeed(0)`), in a struct held inside one too. Of any other default the prover says the code is not read.
Remove-when: The library's prover reads a struct's constructor defaults. `bun run beep patches prove` then says this
  patch's test passes without it.
Test: test/alchemy-domain/05-a-structs-defaults/StructDefaults.test.ts

